What:		/dev/rust-chardev
Date:		September 2026
KernelVersion:	7.2 (local development patch)
Contact:	Local RK3588 Rust driver project
Description:
		A development/test character device. Each open creates a private
		4096-byte FIFO. Duplicated descriptors share the same open file.
		Reads remove bytes; writes append bytes. Empty reads and full
		writes block interruptibly unless O_NONBLOCK is set, in which
		case they return EAGAIN. Transfers may be short, particularly
		at a ring wrap or partial userspace copy. A zero-byte user-copy
		fault returns EFAULT and preserves the FIFO. Zero-length reads
		and writes return zero. poll/epoll report read/write readiness;
		positioned I/O is unsupported (ESPIPE). No private ioctls exist.
		Device permissions follow the default miscdevice policy. An
		open file holds a module reference until final close.
		This device is independent of the board's physical UART/RS485.
